      "skeletal": true,
      "animationValidated": false,
      "reviewPath": "penguin-source-v0670.html",
      "scope": "Qualitative locomotion; 1.47 Hz active cycle referenced to Sato et al. 2010 table 2. No calibrated speed, thrust, energetics, thermoregulation or complete physiology.",
      "description": "Selected Marcel Porsiel feathered exterior with a new bound rig. Choose Walk or Swim to play the movement study. Swimming straightens the body and neck, keeps the belly down and trails both feet; paired flippers settle into a glide. Active stroke cycle: 1.47 Hz from an emperor field study; joint angles and step timing are authored."
